{
  "title": "PyTorch 2.8.0 ONNX export generates boolean values for integer-only allowzero attribute",
  "issue_id": "161941",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\n**Problem:**\nPyTorch 2.8.0 ONNX export incorrectly generates boolean `True` instead of integer `1` for the `allowzero` attribute in Reshape operations, causing downstream serialization failures with onnx-ir.\n\n**Minimal reproducing example:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport warnings\nimport tempfile\nimport os\n\n# CRITICAL: Force DeprecationWarnings to be errors (this triggers the issue!)\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"error\", category=DeprecationWarning)\n\nclass TestModel(nn.Module):\n    def forward(self, x):\n        # This reshape triggers the boolean->int issue\n        return x.reshape(1, -1)\n\nmodel = TestModel().eval()\nx = torch.randn(2, 4)\n\n# Try ONNX export - this should trigger SerdeError\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix='.onnx', delete=False) as f:\n    try:\n        torch.onnx.export(\n            model,\n            (x,),\n            f.name,\n            opset_version=18,\n            dynamo=True,\n            verbose=False\n        )\n        print(\"❌ UNEXPECTED: Export succeeded\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"✅ CONFIRMED: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\")\n    finally:\n        try:\n            os.unlink(f.name)\n        except:\n            pass\n```\n\n**Error:**\n```\nonnx_ir.serde.SerdeError: Error calling serialize_attribute_into with: Attr('allowzero', INT, True)\n```\n\n**Full traceback showing the root cause:**\n```\nFile \"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages/onnx_ir/serde.py\", line 1703, in serialize_node_into\n  serialize_attribute_into(node_proto.attribute.add(), from_=attr)\nonnx_ir.serde.SerdeError: Error calling serialize_attribute_into with: Attr('allowzero', INT, True)\n\nNode(..., attributes={'allowzero': Attr('allowzero', INT, True)}, ...)\n```\n\n**Environment:**\n- **PyTorch**: 2.8.0+cpu\n- **ONNX**: 1.19.0  \n- **onnx-ir**: 0.1.7\n- **Platform**: Linux (Ubuntu 22.04)\n- **Python**: 3.11.0rc1\n- **Protobuf**: 6.32.0\n\n**Root Cause:**\nPyTorch's new dynamo-based ONNX export generates `Attr('allowzero', INT, True)` instead of the ONNX-compliant `Attr('allowzero', INT, 1)`. The ONNX specification requires integer values (0/1) for the allowzero attribute.\n\n**Impact:**\n- Breaks ONNX export for PyTorch Geometric models in CI environments\n- Affects any model using reshape operations with strict warning handling\n- Forces workarounds in downstream projects\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\n`allowzero=True` should serialize as `Attr('allowzero', INT, 1)`\n\n**Actual Behavior:**\n`allowzero=True` serializes as `Attr('allowzero', INT, True)` (boolean in integer field)\n\n\n\n### Versions\n\n\n### **Versions:**\nCollecting environment information...\nPyTorch version: 2.8.0+cpu\nIs debug build: False\nCUDA used to build PyTorch: None\nROCM used to build PyTorch: N/A\n\nOS: Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS (x86_64)\nGCC version: (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04.2) 11.4.0\nClang version: Could not collect\nCMake version: Could not collect\nLibc version: glibc-2.35\n\nPython version: 3.11.0rc1 (main, Aug 12 2022, 10:02:14) [GCC 11.2.0] (64-bit runtime)\nPython platform: Linux-5.15.167.4-microsoft-standard-WSL2-x86_64-with-glibc2.35\nIs CUDA available: False\nCUDA runtime version: No CUDA\nCUDA_MODULE_LOADING set to: N/A\nGPU models and configuration: No CUDA\nNvidia driver version: No CUDA\ncuDNN version: No CUDA\nIs XPU available: False\nHIP runtime version: N/A\nMIOpen runtime version: N/A\nIs XNNPACK available: True\n\nVersions of relevant libraries:\n[pip3] numpy==2.3.2\n[pip3] onnx==1.19.0\n[pip3] onnx-ir==0.1.7\n[pip3] onnxscript==0.4.0\n[pip3] torch==2.8.0+cpu\n[pip3] torch-geometric==2.6.1\n[pip3] torchvision==0.23.0+cpu\n[conda] Could not collect\n\n\ncc @justinchuby @titaiwangms",
